                <pb facs="0133" n="33" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg33"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894c.111/2: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Reinsch</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-04-19T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 19,
                                1918—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your April 6, 7 p.m.</p>
                <p>The Department acquiesces in the application of the passport regulations, made
                    temporarily expedient by the war, to Americans <pb facs="0134" n="34"
                        xml:id="pg34"/> entering Port Arthur leased territory and South Manchuria
                    railroad zone on the understanding that acquiescence does not commit this
                    Government in any respect regarding the relative rights of China and Japan in
                    these districts or regarding the divestment of American citizens in Manchuria of
                    their extraterritorial rights.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
